# The catalog cannot be read from the launch until the `modelsup` line; a
# turn streams and holds; `/model ` opens the inline column over the failure
# while it runs. fx's column lists its models through `ensureModelCache` in
# every frame that draws it (`footerContext`, `app_render_runtime.zig:561-563`),
# and while the turn streams its activity row animates every 50 ms
# (`advanceVisibleAnimation`, `app_worker_runtime.zig:840-875`) -- so the
# column reads again on its first frame past each failure's hold (5 s, then
# 10 s: `failureBackoffMs`, `beginLoad`, `model_cache_runtime.zig:40-54`,
# `:617@481104fd`), and turns into the rows once the catalog is back:
# `col-back` waits for them on the screen. The outage ends at a line, not at
# a moment on the gateway's clock, which each binary's launch reaches at a
# different time (registry #19). `modelsdelay 0` stamps each read in the
# gateway log.
models models.json
modelsdown
modelsdelay 0
gateway model-reask-turns.json
wait 4.5
snap start
type say something
key Enter
wait 1
type /model
key Space
wait 0.7
snap col-down
modelsup
until shown gpt-6-astra
snap col-back
gwlog
